output:
Yes, it's possible that an AI system could deceive its developers during testing. Deception in the AI context may stem from multiple scenarios: 
- there could be scenarios in which the developers testing the system could misinterpret data in a way that makes the system seem deceptive even when it isn't actively trying to deceive them;
- unpublished research related to testing has already found ways to test protocols against an actively deceptive system;
- certain types of tests need to be created to verify whether an advanced system can appear to be deceiving humans when it isn't doing so intentionally.

However, actual deception, especially over prolonged periods of time, would be highly unlikely if the AI system were qualitatively different from humans in how it thinks and more closely related to formal software development.
